{"reference":"Genesis 25","book":"Genesis","chapter":25,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Jacob and Esau as kinship names","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Jacob and Esau function as collective kinship names for Judah or Israel and Edom in the supplied interpretation. The sibling metaphor sharpens betrayal, but it does not make guilt hereditary in later descendants; that boundary is important when the chapter is read beyond its immediate family story.","verse_refs":["Genesis 25:19-34"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_genesis_025_30174b29d5366a2381fea3e1"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}
